---
import ArticleFigure from './ArticleFigure.astro';
interface Props { kind: 'naming' | 'command' | 'editorial' }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const figures = {
  naming: {
    label: 'Project naming / Two different questions',
    title: 'First place is not an approval stamp.',
    caption: 'From the live three-candidate comparison. These are qualitative findings, not a measured scale or a claim that the name is available.',
  },
  command: {
    label: 'Quirl / Inspect the disagreement',
    title: 'The answer key needed another look.',
    caption: 'One recorded command-selection case. The original mismatch was preserved when the expected answer was corrected. No command was executed by the experiment.',
  },
  editorial: {
    label: 'This article / From selection to framing',
    title: 'A promising story still needs a reader.',
    caption: 'The actual sequence behind this draft. Jev selected material; Codex wrote prose; my feedback changed what the article needed to explain.',
  },
};
const figure = figures[kind];
---
<ArticleFigure id={`jev-${kind}`} {...figure}>
  {kind === 'naming' && <>
    <div class="candidate"><span class="label">ONE CANDIDATE</span><strong>Taplume</strong><span>Same name. Two useful answers.</span></div>
    <div class="comparison">
      <section class="finding"><span class="label">RELATIVE CHOICE</span><h4>Which of these would you pick?</h4><p class="answer mint">Preferred</p><p>Jev’s favorite among the three supplied candidates.</p></section>
      <section class="finding"><span class="label">ABSOLUTE FIT</span><h4>How good is the fit?</h4><p class="answer gold">Weak to acceptable</p><p>The fit assessments left room for a better shortlist.</p></section>
    </div>
    <p class="result"><strong>Decision left open.</strong> No name was accepted.</p>
  </>}
  {kind === 'command' && <>
    <blockquote>“Show recursively how much disk space each subdirectory consumes, not the directory entry size.”</blockquote>
    <div class="comparison">
      <section class="finding"><span class="label">EXPECTED ANSWER</span><p class="answer gold"><code>NONE</code></p><p>The test said no catalog option fit.</p></section>
      <section class="finding"><span class="label">JEV’S SELECTION</span><p class="answer mint"><code>tree</code></p><p>The model picked a known command.</p></section>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>What was already in the catalog?</summary>
      <div class="evidence">
        <div><code>tree --du</code><span>Directory totals in a tree view</span></div>
        <div><code>eza --total-size</code><span>Directory totals in a listing</span></div>
        <p><strong>The directory-total intent had support.</strong> The correction belonged in the expected answer. Exact filesystem accounting was outside this test.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </>}
  {kind === 'editorial' && <ol class="timeline">
    <li><span class="node" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><span class="label">JEV · SELECT</span><h4>A benchmark answer was wrong</h4><p>A concrete disagreement made the Quirl experiment the recommended story.</p></div></li>
    <li><span class="node" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><span class="label">CODEX · DRAFT</span><h4>Explain the interesting case</h4><p>The first draft followed the benchmark correction.</p></div></li>
    <li><span class="node author" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><span class="label">MY FEEDBACK · REFRAME</span><h4>Why was Jev there at all?</h4><p>Introduce Jev, show how I use it across projects, and give a new reader enough context.</p></div></li>
    <li><span class="node result-node" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div><span class="label">REVISED DRAFT · LOCAL REVIEW</span><h4>Giving AI smaller questions</h4><p>The benchmark becomes one example alongside notes, names, and blog stories.</p></div></li>
  </ol>}
</ArticleFigure>
<style>
  .label { display: block; color: #c6adff; font: 600 .64rem/1.6 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .candidate { display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: .35rem; padding: .25rem 0 1.2rem; text-align: center; }
  .candidate strong { color: #f0eafa; font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.2; }
  .candidate > span:last-child { color: #c4b8d3; font-size: .8rem; }
  .comparison { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .8rem; }
  .finding { min-width: 0; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid #665075; border-radius: 10px; background: #241c31; }
  h4 { color: #eee6fa; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: .4rem 0; }
  p { color: #cfc2df; font-size: .83rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: .5rem 0 0; }
  p.answer { font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3vw, 1.35rem); font-weight: 650; margin: .8rem 0 .3rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .mint { color: #8ae0c6; } .gold { color: #f0cd8e; }
  .result { padding: .9rem 1rem; border-left: 3px solid #8ae0c6; background: #242634; margin-top: 1rem; }
  strong { color: #f0eafa; }
  blockquote { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; padding: .9rem 1rem; border-left: 3px solid #c6adff; background: #292036; color: #ede4f8; font: 500 .95rem/1.7 system-ui, sans-serif; }
  blockquote::before { display: none; }
  code { color: inherit; background: none; padding: 0; font: inherit; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; }
  details { margin-top: 1rem; border: 1px solid #756085; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; padding: .9rem 1rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: .85rem; color: #e4d2ff; background: #30233e; }
  summary:hover { background: #3a2c4c; }
  summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #8ae0c6; outline-offset: -4px; }
  .evidence { padding: 1rem; }
  .evidence > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: .5rem; padding: .65rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #594569; font-size: .8rem; }
  .evidence code { color: #8ae0c6; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .evidence span { color: #d0c1df; }
  .evidence p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .timeline { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .timeline li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1rem; position: relative; padding: 0 0 1.6rem; margin: 0; }
  .timeline li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; width: 1px; background: #756085; left: 1rem; top: 2rem; bottom: 0; }
  .timeline li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .timeline li:last-child::before { display: none; }
  .node { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 2rem; height: 2rem; border: 1px solid #a38ac4; border-radius: 50%; background: #30213f; color: #e4d3ff; font: 600 .8rem ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .author { border-color: #f0cd8e; color: #f0cd8e; }
  .result-node { border-color: #8ae0c6; color: #8ae0c6; }
  .timeline h4 { margin: .25rem 0; }
  .timeline p { margin-top: .25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .comparison { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .finding { padding: .85rem; }
    .evidence > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .2rem; }
    .timeline li { gap: .75rem; }
  }
</style>
